id: brim/usage
name: honest refusal of clumsy invocation
prose: |
  A bad knob value, an extra file argument, an unknown option, an unknown command, and a missing picture are refused with the offending value named along with its requirement, plus the usage line, on exit code 2.
scope:
- brim
- package.json
- src/**
- material/**
- node_modules/**
covers:
- R1
- R2
- R3
- R4
rows:
- run: ./brim
  expect:
    rc: 2
    out: "contains: missing command"
- run: ./brim detect
  expect:
    rc: 2
    out: "contains: no picture given"
- run: ./brim detect material/bordered.jpg extra.jpg
  expect:
    rc: 2
    out: "contains: extra file argument 'extra.jpg'"
- run: ./brim detect material/bordered.jpg --band 0.7
  expect:
    rc: 2
    out: "contains: bad --band value '0.7': a fraction of the side, greater than 0 and at most 0.5"
- run: ./brim detect material/bordered.jpg --band abc
  expect:
    rc: 2
    out: "contains: bad --band value 'abc': a fraction of the side, greater than 0 and at most 0.5"
- run: ./brim detect material/bordered.jpg --threshold 1.5
  expect:
    rc: 2
    out: "contains: bad --threshold value '1.5': a fraction from 0 to 1"
- run: ./brim detect material/bordered.jpg --wat
  expect:
    rc: 2
    out: "contains: unknown option '--wat'"
- run: ./brim frobnicate x.jpg
  expect:
    rc: 2
    out: "contains: unknown command 'frobnicate'"
